D. TORQUE: THE KING’S GAME

[Body in a field]

Narrator:
“Police called it an accident.”

[Close-up of backpack]

Narrator:
“But Detective D. Torque noticed one thing nobody else did.”

D. Torque:
“That backpack wasn’t luggage.”

D. Torque:
“It was a parachute.”

[Rapid flashes of evidence boards]

Narrator:
“Six cases. Six victims.”

Narrator:
“Everyone thought they were unrelated.”

D. Torque:
“They weren’t.”

[Photos connected with red string]

Narrator:
“Each victim knew part of a secret.”

[Victor Hale silhouette]

Narrator:
“And one man spent years making sure they never put the pieces together.”

Text:
D. TORQUE: THE KING’S GAME

Narrator:
“The king has finally been found.”
